[0m$ [0mcd /home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing-steer2 && git add apps/ledgerline-web/assets/tokens.css apps/ledgerline-web/assets/tokens.json apps/ledgerline-web/assets/ui/switch.css apps/ledgerline-web/assets/ui/sheet.css && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git log --oneline -3
Fix: the last two ramp-step/shadow leaks need token-layer names

The previous steer pass deliberately stopped here: both defects are of the
family the critique flagged, but neither can be fixed by swapping one value
for another, because the correct value is theme-dependent and no token
named it in this tree.

`switch.css` reached for `--ns-paper-12` for the thumb. The paper ramp
inverts, so a thumb that must stay light in both themes cannot be a ramp
step at all: in dark, paper-12 is near-white and the thumb's own 1px ring
(paper-12 at 10%) vanished into it. The comment above the rule already
claimed "deliberately not a ramp step" while the declarations used one —
the intent was recorded and never applied. Now `--ns-control-thumb`
(#ffffff light, var(--ns-paper-12) dark) carries what the comment always
said; the ring mixes `--ns-fg`, which is theme-aware.

`sheet.css` used `--ns-shadow-xl`, which is omnidirectional. A drawer is
docked to an edge and casts away from it, so it needs the direction the
old -8px offset used to carry. Now `--ns-shadow-drawer`.

Both tokens are added to tokens.json (light and dark) and to the generated
tokens.css, with values matching design/ledgerline-ui so the two trees do
not drift. Parity checked programmatically: 175 declared in JSON, 175
defined in CSS, no divergence either way.

Verification: deno task check clean on the app (the aspire group fails only
because aspire/node_modules is absent in this checkout — pre-existing and
present on master too); 42 tests pass; deno fmt --check clean on all four
files. Pre-existing lint debt in register-apps.mts, sagas/runtime.ts,
saga-instances.tsx and daily-maintenance.ts is untouched.
EOF
